Z||000000||1FST2M6||05-11-2000||04:18 PM||||OK someone caught me in a poorly executed equation. I’ve stated that According to Pontiac (GM Performance book) at the local dealer (Carl Black Pontiac) that they claim their driveline loss of 27.5%  I then took the numbers spit out by the dyno took 27.5% of that and added that on. Which is WRONG! I’ve already lost 27.5% why find the percentage of a lesser number when the Flywheel actually makes higher numbers! Thanks a bunch! Ok guys/gals. Once you have your Dyno print out in front of you add 37% of your wheel number that will give you the 27.5% drive line loss… look here  122.1*37%=45.17   122.1+45.17=167.27(actual flywheel HP)   167.27*27.5%=45.99  (actual power loss) I lose almost 46hp in the tranny! what is the Factory given percentage of loss 27.5% of 167 yep 122! That’s my rear wheel number! So I’ve told everyone the WRONG way to find out how much go you have... and I’ve fooled myself into having less hp! Instead of the 155HP I thought I had at the flywheel it’s actually 167HP!!! Just tossing up some numbers for the ones that pay attention…  so my REAL flywheel #s are and these numbers are accurate to about 1 HP and 1LBFT<BR>NO NOS   167HP   &  217 LBFT<BR>ON NOS    224HP  &  323 LBFT <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-11-2000||04:19 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
