Z||000005||1FST2M6||05-12-2000||10:52 AM||||I have 97,141 miles on my current motor. The one that came from the factory in the car!  These numbers are with out my headers and with out the install of my 4:10 tranny that got here Wednesday. I got the 27.5% driveline loss from  “The GM Performance Book” it’s a black book (catalog) with a Goodwrench Funny Car on the front of it at Carl Black Pontiac (Dealer in Kennesaw, Ga.) Even DynoJet says a minimum of 20% driveline loss should be expected. I’m not sure about the torque curve issue.  No change in compression, no internal engine mods at all!  Yep still gunna put a S/C on my new motor not this one. For a list of mods see  <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net/fiero.htm</A>  or <A HREF="http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html</A>   There are too many to type so the link is easier…  I have recently changed from the Crane HI-6s to a MSD 6BTM. It’s a better ignition system and it has the necessary boost retard for the supercharger application.  For the English translation… 2 ½ years at Georgia Tech as an Engineering student and working at an Engineering Firm surrounded by math all day and I still screwed this up. In addition; I’m closer to the magical 200HP then I thought. I’m only 33HP away instead of 45.   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>  if you want to see the Dyno sheet and check my math. Thanks for catching that Taylor!  HEY! Maybe with the introduction of Methanol I’ll fall over the 200 mark!  Hummm… <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 05-12-2000).]||||reg||1
